1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,570
Audit reports say “Fixed”.

2
00:00:01,570 --> 00:00:02,740
Users trust it.

3
00:00:02,740 --> 00:00:06,050
Nobody checks the code that's actually deployed.

4
00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:06,900
FixCheck does.

5
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:13,670
It read 22 checks of 21 findings marked fixed, against the code at each protocol's listed address:

6
00:00:13,670 --> 00:00:18,620
7 fixed, 2 not fixed, and 6 deployed before the audit.

7
00:00:18,667 --> 00:00:24,187
This is PoolTogether: one row per finding, its status, and how it was decided.

8
00:00:24,233 --> 00:00:25,883
This finding was marked fixed.

9
00:00:25,883 --> 00:00:28,843
On the left is the function the auditors reviewed;

10
00:00:28,843 --> 00:00:32,463
on the right, the one deployed on Arbitrum after the audit.

11
00:00:32,463 --> 00:00:34,683
They're identical, line for line.

12
00:00:34,733 --> 00:00:38,283
Against the fix commit, the fixed line simply isn't there.

13
00:00:38,283 --> 00:00:40,983
So code alone says: not fixed.

14
00:00:41,033 --> 00:00:43,573
When code can't decide, validators ask a model,

15
00:00:43,573 --> 00:00:46,433
but it must quote a line the fix added.

16
00:00:46,433 --> 00:00:50,813
Here it couldn't, so the check is inconclusive and everyone is refunded.

17
00:00:50,867 --> 00:00:55,467
To check a finding yourself, pick the report, the finding and the deployed address.

18
00:00:55,467 --> 00:00:59,987
Before you pay, the app runs the same checks the contract will.

19
00:01:00,033 --> 00:01:02,433
Then you stake that it isn't fixed.

20
00:01:02,433 --> 00:01:07,783
Every validator reads the report, both commits, the verified source and the deployment date.

21
00:01:07,833 --> 00:01:10,833
This vault was deployed the day before the audit,

22
00:01:10,833 --> 00:01:13,713
so code already says: predates the audit.

23
00:01:13,767 --> 00:01:15,497
Code decides everything it can.

24
00:01:15,497 --> 00:01:20,587
The model never decides what counts as evidence, the dates, or the money.

25
00:01:20,633 --> 00:01:23,643
The real result: six PoolTogether contracts run the audited

26
00:01:23,643 --> 00:01:26,643
code but predate the audit and can't be upgraded.

27
00:01:26,643 --> 00:01:29,883
Two vaults deployed after it are not fixed.

28
00:01:29,933 --> 00:01:31,473
Code compares the functions.

29
00:01:31,473 --> 00:01:36,483
GenLayer validators only judge the middle cases, and must quote the exact lines.

30
00:01:36,483 --> 00:01:39,583
fixcheck-ledger dot vercel dot app.
